            }
          ],
          "hints": {
            "en": [
              "<p>The present simple is often used with the following words and phrases:</p>\n<p><strong>adverbs</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&bull; always <br />&bull; usually <br />&bull; often<br />&bull; sometimes <br />&bull; rarely <br />&bull; never</p>\n<p><strong>phrases</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&bull; every Monday/week/etc<br />&bull; each Monday/week/etc<br />&bull; once/twice a week/month/etc<br />&bull; three times a week/month/etc</p>",
              "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Remember that these adverbs usually go </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">before the verb, but </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">after </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">the verb </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">be.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">&bull; I </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\"><strong>often</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">play football with </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">my </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">friends.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">&bull; I am </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\"><strong>often</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">late for </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">my </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">piano lessons.</span> </p>"
            ]
          },
          "forms": {
            "statement": [
              "I/you/we/they play ...",
              "He/she/it plays ..."
            ],
            "negative": [
